
======================================================================================================================
k_kernel-shape_clustera1  --  candidate K2a: is the cluster residual a SECOND acceleration constant?
======================================================================================================================

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0.  RESTATEMENT TEST -- executed on the FORMULA, symbolically and then numerically
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Start from the kernel, which is the RAR:      g_obs = nu(g_bar/a1) g_bar,  nu(y) = 1/(1 - exp(-sqrt(y)))
  Divide:                                       g_bar/g_obs = 1 - exp(-sqrt(g_bar/a1))
  Rearrange:                                    sqrt(g_bar/a1) = -ln(1 - g_bar/g_obs)
  Solve:                                        a1 = g_bar [ -ln(1 - g_bar/g_obs) ]^(-2)      QED, 3 lines.
  The derivation CLOSES.  The formula is the RAR solved for its own constant and contains no new physics.
    numerical closure, canonical footing: a1 recovered = 9.360000e-11, 9.360000e-11, 9.360000e-11, 9.360000e-11   (injected 9.360e-11)
    numerical closure, alt       footing: a1 recovered = 1.130000e-10, 1.130000e-10, 1.130000e-10, 1.130000e-10   (injected 1.130e-10)
  [PASS] 0a  the closed form is EXACTLY the kernel inverted -- injecting a0 and reading a1 back must return a0 to machine precision.  This is what makes the FORMULA a restatement
         (max |a1/a0 - 1| = 8.88e-16 over four accelerations and both footings)
  is_restatement: TRUE for the closed form; the two-point DISAGREEMENT below is a measurement, not a
  restatement, and the two must never be quoted as one result.

