----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.  MUTATION CONTROL -- objects BUILT to have one acceleration scale must come back with ratio 1
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    injected a1 = a0 (canonical) at BOTH radii, using each group's own measured baryons: recovered ratio = 1.000000 (spread 8.88e-16)
    injected a1 = a0 (alt) at BOTH radii, using each group's own measured baryons: recovered ratio = 1.000000 (spread 8.47e-16)
  [PASS] 2a  MUTATION CONTROL: the estimator has no ratio of its own -- objects with a single acceleration scale return 1.000000 exactly, so the measured 2.96 cannot be an artefact of the geometry or of the two radii
         (recovered ratio = 1.000000 on both footings, using the real groups' own baryon distributions)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.  THE LambdaCDM ALTERNATIVE, COMPUTED BESIDE -- does an NFW halo give the same ratio?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Build, for each group, an NFW halo of the SAME M500 with a concordance concentration; take R2500 and
  M2500 from the NFW itself; feed it the group's OWN measured gas masses; run the identical estimator.
  If the NFW mock reproduces the measured ratio, the two-point contradiction is a restatement of the
  known cluster problem and not a new fact.
    c500  median R2500/R500  median M2500/M500  median a1 ratio     data
     2.0              0.409              0.342            2.419    3.188
     2.5              0.427              0.390            2.802    3.188
     3.0              0.441              0.430            3.103    3.188
     3.5              0.452              0.463            3.365    3.188
     4.0              0.461              0.490            3.583    3.188
     5.0              0.475              0.534            3.925    3.188
  the DATA's own median R2500/R500 = 0.448 and M2500/M500 = 0.448
  [FAIL] 3a  THE DECISIVE CONTROL, AND IT CAN FAIL: does a concordance NFW halo -- an object with dark matter and no second acceleration scale of any kind -- reproduce the measured two-point ratio?  If it does, the 'kill' is a restatement of the known cluster problem in a new estimator
         (the NFW family spans a1 ratios 2.42 - 3.92 over c500 = 2-5, and the measured 3.19 sits INSIDE that range (closest at c500 = 3.0))

